# =============================================================================
# generate_synthetic_corpus.py  —  Synthetic (label=1) Textual Corpus Builder
# =============================================================================
# PURPOSE:
#   Builds the "vs LLM copy" side of CATEGORY_TEXTUAL_CORPUS (§3.9, Table 3.4).
#   Per seed_sources.py's own documented methodology: "SYNTHETIC (label=1)
#   text must be GENERATED BY YOU deliberately for training purposes... this
#   is the standard, ethical way to build the 'vs LLM copy' side of the
#   corpus... rather than trying to find real-world text that is merely
#   suspected of being AI-written."
#
# WHY THIS BYPASSES THE --label REVIEW QUEUE:
#   Every other sample in this project (scraped news articles, ad videos)
#   needs a human to look at it and judge authentic-vs-synthetic, because
#   the ground truth isn't known until reviewed. These samples are the one
#   exception: the ground truth is certain BY CONSTRUCTION the moment
#   they're generated — there is no "suspected AI text" ambiguity to
#   resolve. So label=1 is set directly, matching the exact same certainty
#   NIT DA/NDPC bureaucratic notices have as label=0 (§3.9's authentic side).
#
# FICTIONAL BRAND NAMES ONLY:
#   All ad-copy samples use invented brands (NaijaConnect, QuickSend,
#   GoldSpring, ZoomRide, MarketNaija) rather than real companies. Real
#   brand names in LLM-generated marketing copy would misleadingly imply
#   those companies produced or endorsed this text — the opposite of what
#   a clean label=1 ground-truth sample needs.
#
# USAGE:
#   python generate_synthetic_corpus.py             # write files + log manifest
#   python generate_synthetic_corpus.py --dry-run   # preview without writing
# =============================================================================

import argparse
